  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Justice obligated $7B in FY2026 to date on federal contracts. The Department of Justice issued 40,892 awards with an average award size of $171K. Obligations are down 18.1% year over year, following a multi-year pattern that shows peak obligations near $10B in FY23 and lower totals in subsequent years. Spending in FY26 to date concentrates in a handful of service and health-related industries, with technology and security among the largest categories by dollars. The top vendor in FY26 to date is METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. at $514M, followed by health and logistics contractors. These figures are contract obligations and reflect fiscal year to date totals that are partial for the current year. Readers should treat FY26 totals as incomplete for the full fiscal year when comparing across years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Justice contract spending changed year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of Justice obligated $7B in FY26 to date, which is down 18.1% year over year. Obligations declined from $10B in FY23 to $9.4B in FY24 and $8.5B in FY25 before the current FY26 to date total. The Department of Justice awarded 40,892 contracts so far in FY26, with an average award size of $171K. Those figures reflect fiscal year to date obligations rather than full-year totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Justice's biggest buying categories and who supplies them?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services, Security Guards and Patrol Services, and General Medical and Surgical Hospitals are the largest NAICS categories in FY26 to date at $826M, $755M, and $645M respectively. The Department of Justice also obligated $469M for Other Residential Care Facilities and $381M for Computer Systems Design Services. METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. is the top vendor at $514M, with NAPHCARE LLC at $185M and MCKESSON CORPORATION at $157M among the leading suppliers."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Justice spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Justice obligated $7B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Justice issued 40,892 awards with an average award size of $171K. Obligations are down 18.1% year over year and FY26 totals are fiscal year to date only."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Justice buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Justice buys technology, security, medical, care, and telecom services. Other Computer Related Services accounted for $826M, Security Guards and Patrol Services accounted for $755M, and General Medical and Surgical Hospitals accounted for $645M in FY26 to date. The Department of Justice also obligated $469M for Other Residential Care Facilities and $381M for Computer Systems Design Services."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Justice's largest contractors?",
      "a": "METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. is the largest contractor at $514M in FY26 to date. NAPHCARE LLC follows at $185M and MCKESSON CORPORATION follows at $157M. Other top vendors include AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC at $149M, THE GEO GROUP, INC. at $145M, and CGI FEDERAL INC. at $138M."
    }
